WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Speaker 1: All right. Let's start today&nbsp;
with news out of Russia and Ukraine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:10.020
These headlines are sort of unbelievable. I've&nbsp;
been stopped short of calling them Kafkaesque,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:15.000
but it's almost appropriate. The Associated&nbsp;
Press reports that Vladimir Putin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.380
the Russian president, has declared martial&nbsp;
law in the annexed regions of Ukraine. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:28.680
that headline might make sense if that there&nbsp;
was really an annexation that took place. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:36.240
we're really talking about is occupied regions of&nbsp;
Ukraine in which Putin is claiming sovereignty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.060
but in which there really is no sovereignty.&nbsp;
And so it's kind of a weird thing to say. I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.380
declaring martial law in parts of a different&nbsp;
country, which is fundamentally what Putin is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.520
doing. But of course, his perspective would be a&nbsp;
different one. Let's look at a little bit of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.660
article and we'll talk about the reasons for this&nbsp;
and the implications and sort of what comes next.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.660
Associated Press Once again, Russian President&nbsp;
Vladimir Putin declared martial law Wednesday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.280
in the four regions of Ukraine that Moscow&nbsp;
annexed and gave additional emergency powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.740
to the heads of all regions of Russia. Putin&nbsp;
didn't immediately spell out the steps that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.020
would be taken under martial law. I think we&nbsp;
can guess some of them, but said his order was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:22.260
effective starting Thursday. His decree gives law&nbsp;
enforcement agencies three days to submit specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:29.640
proposals and orders the creation of territorial&nbsp;
defense forces in those four annexed regions. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:36.840
the statement here from Putin, again, it's it's&nbsp;
all extremely dystopian. Quote, We are working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:44.460
to solve very difficult, large scale tasks to&nbsp;
ensure Russia's security and safe future to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:51.660
protect our people. Those who are on the front&nbsp;
lines are undergoing training at firing ranges,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:57.240
and training centers should feel our support&nbsp;
and know that they have our big great country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.980
and unified people behind their back.&nbsp;
Sounds a little bit Trumpy, quite frankly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.600
The Associated Press article also adds The&nbsp;
upper house of Russia's parliament was set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.160
to quickly seal Putin's decision to impose&nbsp;
martial law. Again, the regions we're talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:18.300
about are Donetsk, Kherson, Luhansk and Zappa&nbsp;
is here. Draft legislation indicates it may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.260
involve restrictions on travel and public&nbsp;
gatherings, tighter censorship and broader&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.980
authority for law enforcement agencies.&nbsp;
Think about the evil genius of this write&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:32.940
up. It's not even your country. You say, Oh&nbsp;
yeah, we're annexing these parts of the country.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:39.780
It's not formally done. And I understand that&nbsp;
when a country is annexing part of another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:45.420
the idea of formality, often what you're talking&nbsp;
about is just years of it sort of being under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:50.520
the control. And then you say, Well, I guess&nbsp;
now it's kind of annexed. That definitely has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.800
not happened. And then you say now that this is&nbsp;
part of our country and we've annexed this, we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.620
going to impose further restrictions and further&nbsp;
repress and suppress reporting from the area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:08.340
etc.. The belief there's a few different beliefs,&nbsp;
sort of like most likely lowest hanging fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:16.500
priorities here. One would be legal cover for&nbsp;
the wave of repressions that are certainly that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:23.220
is certainly to come as absurd as that cover is.&nbsp;
Hey, this is Russia now. And so now we're imposing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:28.680
martial law. The other aspect of this and a couple&nbsp;
of people wrote to me said, you know, David, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:35.460
kind of silly to say you're like imposing martial&nbsp;
law in any kind of formal way because it's a war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:42.720
zone. And so by definition, it's all kind of under&nbsp;
the control, at least ostensibly of the military.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:48.420
So to now declare the martial law, it's it kind&nbsp;
of is under a de facto martial law type situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:56.340
because it's militaries fighting each other. We're&nbsp;
looking at a forced mobilization of Ukrainians in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:04.980
the area to start getting the Ukrainians out.&nbsp;
And this is by many reasonable assessments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:12.120
a war crime. But by pretending that this is now&nbsp;
Russia, that these four regions are part of Russia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:18.120
and that the individuals there are Russian,&nbsp;
because remember, he's, quote, annexed it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:27.420
It's I don't I don't want to call it plausible,&nbsp;
but it's sort of is a 1% attempt at claiming that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:34.740
what you're doing is just the governance of your&nbsp;
own country rather than an alleged war crimes. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.420
it's bonkers and it's crazy. And of course,&nbsp;
we continue to wonder about what is the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:46.080
game here. There does not seem to be a face saving&nbsp;
offramp for Vladimir Putin here. And increasingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:53.160
the questions among the United States and Western&nbsp;
allies continue to be how far do we allow this to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:59.520
go and for how long? And what are the sort of red&nbsp;
lines at which point different interventions would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:07.020
happen for how long and to what degree and in what&nbsp;
particular ways do we again use Western allies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.980
naito, etc.? Sort of these Venn Venn circles&nbsp;
of those individual groups continue to fund and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:23.100
supply Ukraine and. At what point do we imagine&nbsp;
that the circumstances may change? And there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:28.740
aren't really good answers to that in the U.S.,&nbsp;
as is often the case. The conversation becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:35.460
what I call toxically partizan. And what I mean&nbsp;
by that is, of course, if different individuals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.960
with different worldviews would have different&nbsp;
opinions about what should be done in Russia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:45.240
obviously more isolationist individuals would&nbsp;
say, we should do nothing. We shouldn't even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:49.140
send money sent note don't send arms and nothing&nbsp;
at all. Don't send legs, don't send anything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:56.760
That's a joke, by the way. Others would say, well,&nbsp;
we we send money, but not arms or we send money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:01.260
and arms, but absolutely nothing beyond that.&nbsp;
Well, what about training? And then, of course, at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:05.640
the very far end of that would be sort of boots on&nbsp;
the ground. The unfortunate thing is that when I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:10.740
say it's become toxically partizan, you have many&nbsp;
right wingers who seek only to attack Joe Biden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:15.720
who take the position that Biden is just wasting&nbsp;
money in Ukraine. Now, a lot of these same people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:21.660
earlier were saying Biden hasn't done enough to&nbsp;
protect the Ukrainian people and Russia never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:28.020
would have even invaded if Trump was president.&nbsp;
So you can't really get anywhere with about 60 to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:34.200
70% of people on this issue. I'm really willing to&nbsp;
entertain reasonable perspectives. I don't want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:38.880
say from both sides, but regardless of political&nbsp;
ideology, I'm willing to entertain reasonable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:45.600
perspectives that will both not allow Russia to&nbsp;
just walk all over whoever they want to walk over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.700
while also not committing or involving&nbsp;
the United States in a way that would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:57.780
either counter counterproductive or not&nbsp;
particularly appropriate, given that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:02.940
should not be the world's police. Any I'm willing&nbsp;
to entertain any reasonable ideas that fall under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:07.080
that umbrella. If you have any as to what&nbsp;
this should look like, feel free to email me.

